Don't check dlls/ns.so in the file consistency check.

With mp_consistency 1 the server compares precached files with each
player's copy. Players have the release ns.so; this server runs its own
build of the same source, which can't match byte for byte, so every player
was kicked with "Bad file (dlls/ns.so) Your NS version differs from the
server's". Clients never load ns.so. cl_dlls/client.{dll,so} and
dlls/ns.dll (release copies, see builder/Dockerfile) are still checked.

--- a/main/source/dlls/client.cpp
+++ b/main/source/dlls/client.cpp
@@ -1209,7 +1209,10 @@
 	// Waste of memory, but files must be precached for the hash check to work.
 	PRECACHE_UNMODIFIED_GENERIC("dlls/ns.dll");
 	PRECACHE_UNMODIFIED_GENERIC("cl_dlls/client.dll");
-	PRECACHE_UNMODIFIED_GENERIC("dlls/ns.so");
+	// Not checked: the server binary is built from source by ns-classic and
+	// can't match the release ns.so byte for byte. Clients never load it; the
+	// client libraries still enforce the release version.
+	//PRECACHE_UNMODIFIED_GENERIC("dlls/ns.so");
 	PRECACHE_UNMODIFIED_GENERIC("cl_dlls/client.so");
 	//PRECACHE_UNMODIFIED_GENERIC("gl_shaders/fs_world.frag");
 	//PRECACHE_UNMODIFIED_GENERIC("gl_shaders/vs_world.vert");
